---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../data/downloads'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Beatport Analyst"
  description="Beatport Analyst keeps track analysis on your device. No extension accounts, no telemetry, no project backend."
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <header class="privacy__header">
      <p class="privacy__eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="privacy__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy__lede">
        Beatport Analyst is a local browser extension. Track data stays in your
        browser. Last updated 6 November 2026.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy__body">
      <section>
        <h2>What data the extension handles</h2>
        <p>
          While you use it on Beatport list pages, the extension may temporarily
          hold track metadata already shown or loaded by Beatport (title,
          artists, mix, BPM, key, label, genre, dates, exclusive/hype flags,
          preview URLs), the page URL and title, and your key-notation
          preference.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How data is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Live snapshots use browser session storage, keyed per Beatport tab,
          and clear when the session ends. Key notation is stored in local
          extension storage on your device. Nothing is synced through cloud sync
          APIs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How data is used</h2>
        <p>
          Only to power the side-panel brief, charts, filters, table, in-panel
          preview playback, and optional CSV export you trigger. The CSV is
          saved locally by your browser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Network activity</h2>
        <p>
          The extension runs only on <code>*.beatport.com</code>. It does not
          call a Beatport partner API or any backend belonging to this project.
          Preview playback may request Beatport media URLs Beatport already
          exposes for that track.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The extension package does not embed analytics, crash reporting, or
          advertising SDKs. This marketing site may load analytics only when
          measurement IDs are configured; that is independent of the extension
          and does not receive extension track snapshots.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Track snapshots are not uploaded, sold, or shared with third parties
          by the extension.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Session snapshots end when the tab or browser session ends. Clear
          extension data or uninstall to remove local preferences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If storage or network behavior changes in a way that affects privacy,
          this page will be updated with a new “last updated” date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions:
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          Canonical markdown copy in the repository:
          <a href="https://github.com/ilyatitovich/bp-analyst/blob/main/PRIVACY.md">
            PRIVACY.md
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .privacy {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: calc(var(--space-8) + 4rem) var(--space-10);
      max-inline-size: 42rem;
    }

    .privacy__eyebrow {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-fg-subtle);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .privacy__title {
      margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .privacy__lede {
      margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
      color: var(--color-fg-muted);
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .privacy__body {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-7);
    }

    .privacy__body h2 {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .privacy__body p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-fg-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .privacy__body a {
      color: var(--color-accent);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    }

    .privacy__body code {
      font-size: 0.92em;
      color: var(--color-fg);
    }
  }
</style>
